WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
The Bank of England was founded in 1694.

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:06.950
The US Federal Reserve, in 1913.

3
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.290
The European Central Bank, in 1998.

4
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.920
Each is a bank.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.220
Each sits at the centre of
a country's money system.

6
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.850
Yet if you walk in and
ask to open an account,

7
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.350
you'll be turned away.

8
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.470
So why can't you open an
account at a central bank,

9
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.430
and what does it do instead?

10
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.680
In this mission, you'll map
the jobs a central bank does,

11
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.040
one by one.

12
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.850
Then you'll open its toolbox,

13
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.670
and see how it steers interest
rates across the whole economy.

14
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: find out what
a central bank is really for.
